{"id": "EUVD-2026-82247", "enisaUuid": "5ba40804-5382-3752-97bb-9c3401baf8af", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/mes: Fix hung_queue_db_array loop limit for multi-XCC\n\nThe loop iterated only AMDGPU_MAX_MES_PIPES times, leaving entries\nuninitialized for multi-XCC GPUs. This causes null pointer dereferences\nwhen accessing arrays indexed by XCC ID >= 2. Extend the loop to cover\nall XCCs (AMDGPU_MAX_MES_PIPES * num_xcc), matching other per-XCC\narrays.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ff668cfc3960ed5b944ac35129f18a15ea08b74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c256086a363f01f9840a57949506eccf5c990a6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93139", "GHSA-h628-62x6-4jjj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "043cdcc2-f752-3499-8a6f-73264f3ef8f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a132fc9bc2f8b394a2f75947a0e1f5c22482a94c <2c256086a363f01f9840a57949506eccf5c990a6"}, {"id": "0560351d-92a0-3615-a890-57291653aebb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "12ac778d-11dd-3fe9-9437-99298255eea8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "59c562b8-3a2c-346a-bdef-4dc52e5f2215", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a132fc9bc2f8b394a2f75947a0e1f5c22482a94c <7ff668cfc3960ed5b944ac35129f18a15ea08b74"}, {"id": "b80869cc-1c06-3954-bf75-c73f213311fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "e9f3abdf-08f1-397e-8864-c5071fdd2341", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d91784fd-c35e-3175-8338-27d236cc5523", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}